userContent.text:
Build an interactive figure using SVG.js.

CONCEPT: A nuclear chain reaction becomes self-sustaining only when the fissile mass is large enough that neutrons are more likely to trigger further fissions than to escape the material.
KEY INSIGHT (what students should walk away understanding): The threshold for a sustained chain reaction is geometric: it is the point where the volume of target nuclei is large enough to capture neutrons before they can cross the surface area to escape.
DEMO STEPS: 4 guided steps — implement the step player in #ui

FULL BLUEPRINT:
{
  "concept": "A nuclear chain reaction becomes self-sustaining only when the fissile mass is large enough that neutrons are more likely to trigger further fissions than to escape the material.",
  "figureType": "diagram",
  "elements": [
    "Blue circular area representing the fissile material",
    "Incoming trigger neutron (small grey sphere)",
    "Fission event markers (gold starbursts)",
    "Neutron trajectory paths (black arrows)",
    "Dynamic status label ('Sub-critical mass' or 'Critical mass')"
  ],
  "interactions": [
    {
      "id": "massSlider",
      "type": "slider",
      "label": "Fissile mass",
      "range": [
        1,
        10,
        1
      ],
      "default": 3,
      "teaches": "Increasing the mass (and therefore radius) decreases the surface-to-volume ratio, reducing the fraction of neutrons that can reach the boundary and escape."
    },
    {
      "id": "triggerReaction",
      "type": "button",
      "label": "Trigger reaction",
      "states": [
        "idle",
        "running",
        "done"
